data: {"type":"response.reasoning_text.done","item_id":"rs_resp_c638c55c107e4b7b968b70120b6be9a2","output_index":0,"text":"\nWe need n divisible by 12, n has exactly 12 positive divisors, find smallest such n.\n\nn divisible by 12 = 2^2 · 3, so n = 2^2 · 3 · m.\n\nNumber of divisors = 12. Possible factorizations of 12: 12 = 12 → p^11; 12 = 6·2 → p^5·q; 12 = 4·3 → p^3·q^2; 12 = 3·2·2 → p^2·q·r.\n\nn must have 2^2 and 3^1 at least.\n\nOptions:\n- p^2·q·r: 2^2·3·r with r prime ≠ 2,3: smallest r = 5 → n = 60. Divisors: (2+1)(1+1)(1+1) = 12. ✓ 60 divisible by 12. So n = 60.\n\nCheck: 60 = 2^2·3·5, divisors count 3·2·2 = 12. Yes.\n\nAnswer: 60.\n","sequence_number":90,"content_index":0}

